  "Question": "Two fair dice are rolled simultaneously. Player A wins if the sum is 7; Player B wins if the sum is 6 or 8; otherwise, neither player wins. How would you describe this game?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "It favors Player A",
    "B": "It is fair",
    "C": "It cannot be determined",
    "D": "It favors Player B"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "There are 6 outcomes with a sum of 7, 5 with a sum of 6, and 5 with a sum of 8, giving 10 outcomes for the latter two sums combined. Player A's probability of winning is \\(6/36\\), and Player B's is \\(10/36\\). Player B has the greater probability, so the game favors Player B.",
